    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting an elite 83.29 score. His matchup against Alcantara is the highest-value spot on the board, driven by a strong platoon advantage and a premium leadoff spot that maximizes his multi-category upside. Similarly, **Josh Lowe** (72.21) and **Nolan Schanuel** (69.91) are high-efficiency plays against Fedde; **Josh Lowe** specifically remains a priority target due to his elite sprint speed against a slow-delivering pitcher, which significantly elevates his stolen base floor despite his lower position in the order. We are also capitalizing on high-ceiling matchups for **Miguel Vargas** (66.33), **Heliot Ramos** (66.80), and **Josh Jung** (66.89), all of whom benefit from favorable park factors and high-ERA opposition, essentially turning their matchups into \"green light\" scenarios for production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Marcell Ozuna** (62.50) on the bench. While his score is robust and higher than several starters, our optimization model favored the specific categorical scarcity\u2014namely stolen bases\u2014provided by **Heliot Ramos** and **Josh Lowe**. **Marcell Ozuna** provides reliable power, but in a 5x5 Roto format, the high-probability speed opportunities presented by the OF starters outweighed the pure run-production value of **Marcell Ozuna** today. Investors should note that **Jacob Wilson** faces a tighter path to value against S\u00e1nchez, as his score of 55.30 is suppressed by the pitcher\u2019s skill level, making him our highest-risk start. We are monitoring the weather closely, as the wind-out conditions boosting players like **Miguel Vargas** and **Jackson Merrill** could easily swing their actual output beyond their current projections.",
